			<div class="head">
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4837494">
																	<a href="/forum/t-13895894/scp-5832#post-4837494">Re: SCP-5832</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607221198" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;" >JamaisJ</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607221102 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2020 02:18</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13895894/scp-5832">SCP-5832</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837494">
									

<p>1) You don't need to make it an SCP; once it demonstrates anomalous attributes it's a given. Also, it feels that this has not been greenlighted but it already has a number.</p>
<p>2) The Red Paper Castle: It may be better to phrase it such that the red paper was transformed into a duplicate of the original castle. I know it's semantics, but it just feels better. You may want to go through and look for similar instances; there are a number of similarly bulky phrasing.</p>
<p>3) This is a good start, but it needs to be expanded upon. Do they have a history? Why did they automatically become enemies, with no apparent attempt at diplomacy? Where are they getting more paper to build the castle? If I put a pack of white paper near the castle, what would happen? Did they have a religion prior to the researcher? What form does that worship take?</p>
<p>Heck, what's the psychology of the castle dwellers? Is it based off real medieval people or an idealized form, such as the SCA? For that matter, why was it built in the first place, was it for a warg game or just to see what could happen?</p>
<p>Again, really cool start. Now flesh it out.</p>

							</div>

								
					
