			<div class="head">
								<div class="title" id="post-title-4837492">
																	<a href="/scp-5762/comments/show#post-4837492"></a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/monteparnas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2926286); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2926286&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607221198" alt="Monteparnas" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2926286)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/monteparnas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2926286); return false;" >Monteparnas</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607220996 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Dec 2020 02:16</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-5762/comments/show">SCP-5762</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837492">
									

<p>Downvote for me, sorry.</p>
<p>The concept is good and its core, the logs, was well done. As a general narrative I have no qualms.</p>
<p>But I think a lot of aspects from the Foundation got lost for no reason:</p>
<p>1- This is not Neutralized, since it still works, it is just depressed;<br />
2- It shouldn't be in a Standard Containment, first because it is an SCP, secondly because it is Sentient and self-motile;<br />
3- The description cuts right to &quot;it Anderson's, so that's why it is anomalous&quot;, giving unnecessary context without describing it or it properties in any relevant way. It sounds like a Task Force report, not the finished article;<br />
4- A lot of details on GOIs' activities that have no bearing in the story and I don't really care;<br />
5- They do no test whatsoever, then someone wants to use it because why not.</p>
<p>Let me be clear, I have nothing against the Foundation deciding to use an anomaly whose effects are actually useful and understood enough for some safety and reliability. But without tests there is no safety and reliability in it. This thing is a frigging autonomous AI, it could do horrible shit out of the blue for unknown reasons, at the very least, without some tests.</p>
<p>Some logs could be those tests, by the way, at least some of them. A single dummy test isn't nearly enough, and even downplaying the dumb &quot;lets fry D-Classes for cheap data&quot;a surgeon just begs for tests with D-Classes that needed the surgery because of accidents and stuff.</p>
<p>As a general concept we already have SCP-2295 and, with a different area of work, SCP-1230. So the good parts aren't enough for not downvoting.</p>

							</div>

								
					
