														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4837481">
									

<p>2) If you are going to make this the first, then you may want to include a way for it to be neutralized, and not just temporarily. Also, no fear of death is likely to create an SCP that is going to be a lot rougher and therefore be harder to contain. The GOI in question may have actually been in the right.</p>
<p>If there does seem to be more of these, then it's possible that The Foundation may assign an MTF or two if they become a major problem.</p>
<p>3) If the phantom simply possesses another car then there is no reason for the memories to carry over; it's the same entity so it would have the same memories. If the phantom died or there was some sort of hive mentality I could see a reason for the note, but since it's not a reincarnation, a new phantom. or otherwise a new entity there's no reason for the note.</p>

							</div>

								
					
